Second race (V3.2) crashed again in the SAME corner: damage 214 at distFromStart ~2468 m, 67.7 s.                       
Telemetry: telemetry/torcs_v3_physics_20261015-105228/ticks.csv. Steering no longer oscillates (good), but steps        
3255-3303 show                                                                                                          
the car NOT braking (brake 0.0, accel ~0.2) while track9 falls from 19.6 m to 2 m at ~100-117 km/h.                     
                                                                                                                        
Read the data and confirm or refute this diagnosis:                                                                     
 (a) V_CORNER is derived from the weighted aim angle; seen from the entry, this hairpin's open road is                  
     only ~15-20 deg off-axis, so V_CORNER comes out ~120-125 km/h and the target speed stays above                     
     the actual speed: no braking.                                                                                      
 (b) The STRAIGHT_DIST bypass (target = V_MAX when d >= 100 m) is physically unsafe: the range sensors                  
     see at most 200 m, and stopping from 230 km/h to a hairpin speed at 7 m/s^2 needs ~280 m.                          
                                                                                                                        
Make V3.3 with the smallest changes:                                                                                    
1. Remove the STRAIGHT_DIST bypass from the target-speed model: always use                                              
   v_target = min(V_MAX, sqrt(V_CORNER^2 + 2 * BRAKE_DECEL * d)). (Keep STRAIGHT_DIST only for the                      
   steering gain.) The 200 m sensor range then caps the safe top speed automatically.                                   
2. Make V_CORNER conservative and independent of the misleading aim angle: V_CORNER = V_CORNER_MIN                      
   (new PARAM, 55 km/h) plus a bonus only when BOTH side rays at +-30 deg are long (wide-open bend):                    
   up to V_CORNER_BONUS (new PARAM, 35 km/h). Remove V_CORNER_SHARP / V_CORNER_FAST.                                    
3. Brake proportionally to the speed excess: brake = clip((speed - target) / BRAKE_RANGE, 0, 1) with                    
   BRAKE_RANGE 15 km/h, still subject to ABS.                                                                           
   Update the self-test (add: wall 15 m ahead at 105 km/h must produce brake > 0) and run it.                           
   Append V3.3 to CHANGELOG.md with the evidence. Do not run the race or invent lap times.                              

