V3.3 is in src/torcs_v3_physics.py (src/torcs_v3_physics.py) and the self-test passes (7 cases). Of your two diagnoses, 
(a) is confirmed in mechanism but not in the numbers, and (b) is correct as physics but did not cause this crash. I did 
not run the race and quote no lap times.                                                                                
                                                                                                                        
What the telemetry shows                                                                                                
                                                                                                                        
The CSV logs only track9, not the other rays, so some of this is back-solved.                                           
                                                                                                                        
- The crash: damage 214 first appears at step 3315, 2468.2 m, 67.68 s. Speed drops from 95 to 17 km/h in one tick.      
- Steps 3255–3303: the brake was above 0 in only 1 of 49 ticks (0.12 at step 3255). Mean accel was about 0.18. track9   
  fell from 19.6 m to 0.3 m while speed only fell from 116.6 to 97.5 km/h.                                              
- Steering: it is saturated at 1.0 from step 3276 and the car runs wide, with trackPos going from 0.46 to −1.0. That    
  fits a car going too fast for the radius, not oscillation.                                                            
                                                                                                                        
(a) Confirmed in mechanism.                                                                                             
- Undoing the V3.2 throttle formula for steps 3256–3300 gives a target only 0–4 km/h above actual speed. That puts      
  V_CORNER at about 96–100 km/h, not 120–125.                                                                           
- That implies an aim angle of roughly 45–50° at those ticks, not 15–20°.                                               
- I can't check the angle at corner entry, because the CSV has no side rays.                                            
- Either way the target stayed just above speed, so the brake never engaged.                                            
- With V_CORNER = 55 the target at d = 19.6 m is about 81 km/h. At 116 km/h that gives brake 1.0.                       
                                                                                                                        
(b) Correct physics, but not the cause here.                                                                            
- Stopping from 230 to 55 km/h at 7 m/s² needs about 275 m, more than the 200 m sensor range.                           
- In steps 3145–3315, track9 never exceeded 94.3 m, so the bypass was most likely not active. The bypass tests the max  
  of rays 8–10, so track9 is indicative, not proof.                                                                     
- The car arrived at 128–144 km/h, not 230.                                                                             
- The bypass is still a latent hazard on faster approaches. Removing it was reasonable, but it would not have prevented 
  this crash.                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
Changes in V3.3                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
- Target speed: the STRAIGHT_DIST bypass is gone. The target is always min(V_MAX, sqrt(Vc² + 2·BRAKE_DECEL·d)).         
  STRAIGHT_DIST now only sets the steering gain. The 200 m range caps the target at about 198 km/h with V_CORNER = 55,  
  and about 211 km/h with the full bonus.                                                                               
- V_CORNER: it is V_CORNER_MIN (55 km/h) plus up to V_CORNER_BONUS (35 km/h). The bonus scales with the shorter of the  
  −30° and +30° rays divided by 200 m. V_CORNER_SHARP and V_CORNER_FAST are removed.                                    
- Brake: clip((speed − target) / BRAKE_RANGE, 0, 1) with BRAKE_RANGE = 15 km/h. This replaces the old -diff/25 + 0.1    
  formula and the "full brake if excess > BRAKE_DECEL·0.5 m/s" rule. ABS is unchanged.                                  
                                                                                                                        
Self-test                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
- Case 6, wall 15 m ahead at 105 km/h: target is 77.7 km/h and brake is 1.00. My first version of this case failed      
  because zero wheel-spin made ABS cut the brake to 0. I fixed the test input to give rolling wheels at 105 km/h, not   
  the driver.                                                                                                           
- Case 7, 200 m free at 230 km/h: target is 210.7 km/h, below V_MAX. I added this case to check that the bypass is gone.
                                                                                                                        
CHANGELOG.md (CHANGELOG.md) has a V3.3 entry with this evidence, including the correction to (a)'s numbers and the      
finding on (b).                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
Risks                                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
- Straight speed and lap time will probably drop because of the 200 m cap and V_CORNER_MIN = 55.                        
- BRAKE_DECEL = 7 m/s² is still an estimate, not a measured value.                                                      
- Downshifts will be more frequent. shift_gears is called with braking=(brake > 0), and the brake now engages on any    
  speed excess.                                                                                                         
- If you want to confirm the entry-side aim angle, log the −30° and +30° rays, track[4] and track[14], in the telemetry.
